<ArticleLayout title="The Verified Homeowner Quote Project" description="A transparent foundation for future installed-cost evidence, with no fabricated submissions or averages." category="Cost" categoryHref="/cost/" published="2026-10-05" updated="2026-10-05" verified="2026-10-05" readingTime="8 min read" toc={[]} sources={sources}>

<h2>Real homeowner quote database coming as verified submissions are collected.</h2><p>There are currently <strong>zero verified homeowner submissions</strong> in this database. We do not publish synthetic quotes as real projects, infer local averages from equipment prices, or turn an unverified total into an installed-cost benchmark.</p>
<h2>What a useful submission needs</h2><p>Future records will capture metro or partial ZIP, state, quote date, exact generator and fuel, ATS, service size, gas-run length, trenching, pad, load management, permits, utility work, electrical upgrades, accessories and project total. Verification status and missing scope must remain visible alongside any future statistics.</p>
<h2>Collection is not open yet</h2><p>No quote-upload form is active. Before collection opens, the service needs authenticated administration, private document storage, malware and file-type checks, rate limits, server-side schema validation, consent records, redaction, a retention policy and a correction/deletion process. Names, addresses, account numbers and original documents must not appear in public records.</p>
<p>The <a href="/planning/quotes/">three-quote tool</a> is available now. It saves only when requested, in your own browser; it does not submit a quote to this project.</p>
<h2>How future comparisons should work</h2><p>Only verified, consented, redacted records should enter a published analysis. Report sample size, date range, geography, configuration mix and missing scope. Separate quotes from completed invoices and changes after installation. Small or biased samples cannot establish a universal fair price.</p>

</ArticleLayout>